Finally, after every change was committed, you have to push the Git Worktree `git push -u origin HEAD`

Examples:

- `git commit -m "✅ feat: new API service Public/OrganizationController@createScammer" -m "Co-Authored-By: Cursor Grok 4.7 <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
- `git commit -m "🛠️ fix: service Admin/OrganizationController@deleteOrganization wasn't working" -m "Co-Authored-By: Cursor Grok 4.7 <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
- `git commit -m "💻 wip: new architecture improvement along Clean Architecture" -m "Co-Authored-By: Cursor Grok 4.7 <cursoragent@cursor.com>`

## Creating the Pull Request

We have to use `gh` command to create the pull request.

```bash
gh pr create --fill -B <target-branch> -H <head-branch>
```

Where `<target-branch>` is the branch where the changes will be merged and `<head-branch>` the branch we are currently.
The response would be the following:

```bash
Warning: 1 uncommitted change

Creating pull request for feature/add-scammer-to-organization into main in Fraude-Bot/Backend

https://github.com/Fraude-Bot/Backend/pull/45
```

Return the pull request url.


